ff on backstroke in the final. Her 1:01.03 split had her over 1½ seconds ahead of the USA’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/50959"} "Beth Barr"] " and the race for gold was over. East Germany increased their margin on each leg, winning in 4:03.74, the second fastest time ever. The USA was well back for silver, finishing in 4:07.90, but that was also almost three seconds ahead of the Canadians, who finished third. The East German victory gave Kristin Otto her fifth gold medal in Seoul. She would later win a sixth in the 50 free."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "East Germany"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GDR.png"}] "GDR"]] [:td {} "4:08.53 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "4:03.74 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "Backstroke"] [:td {:class "bib"} "177"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47512"} "Kristin Otto"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "Breaststroke"] [:td {:class "bib"} "172"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47482"} "Silke Hörner"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "Butterfly"] [:td {:class "bib"} "183"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47555"} "Birte Weigang"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "Freestyle"] [:td {:class "bib"} "174"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47503"} "Katrin Meißner"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "Backstroke"] [:td {:class "bib"} "180"] [:td {} [:a {:hr